correction('P000550','polynomial Wronskian normalization',r'\(P_xQ-Q_xP-2i\zeta PQ=\prod(\zeta-\zeta_j)\)',r'Supply leading factor \(-2ipq\), and reconcile exponential signs',r'For leading coefficients \(p,q\), the left side has leading coefficient \(-2ipq\). The earlier pair \(Pe^{+i\zeta x},Qe^{-i\zeta x}\) has the opposite sign in this Wronskian convention.','faithful_error')
correction('P000550','Riccati spectral shift and Miura coefficients',r'\(f_x+f^2=q\), plus-sign equations with coefficient 3',r'For \(-y_{xx}+Vy=\zeta^2y\): \(f_x+f^2=V-\zeta^2\); use a consistently normalized Miura identity',r'The exact conditional identity is given in boundary row 1973-330.11. The overwritten sign and time scaling do not permit a unique literal replacement.','ambiguity')
correction('P000552','Laplacian sign',r'Positive spectrum and \(\exp(-t\Delta)\), but coordinate \(\operatorname{div}\operatorname{grad}\)',r'Use \(L=-\operatorname{div}\operatorname{grad}\) for positive eigenvalues, or reverse spectrum and heat signs','The scan is cancelled before the coordinate expression; sign consistency is clear mathematically but the original cancelled sign is not recoverable.','ambiguity')
